Z||000025||BN Boomer||09-02-99||10:02 PM||||Greg, Age 31<BR>Puget Sound, WA<BR>Railroad worker<P>I bought my first Fiero, an 87 SC, 2 1/2 months ago for $300. It was sitting in a farmer's field and the 2.5L had a knocking rod. After a little looking around, I contacted forum member SCCA FIERO and he gave me a decent running 88 2.5L for free. So factoring in the gas to drive to Utah and back for the engine along with a few odds and ends needed in the engine swap, I'm into it for less than $600. Everyone who sees it thinks I got a hell of a deal.<P><p>[This message has been edited by BN Boomer (edited 09-08-1999).]||||||
Z||000026||88 Fiero||09-02-99||11:09 PM||||Hello...my name is Gabriel in Upland, California... I am 34 yrs. old... and working as a Network Partner Consultant...My passion for Fiero's started back in 1984 and bought my first Fiero 2M4 in 1985..Put about 80,000 wonderful miles on it for 2 yrs. and sold it for a '85 4-speed V6 SE...Love the car but I want more...So after I sold my '85 I bought a  1988 Formula 5 speed... I converted the car to the GT fastback...I paid $3,000 and the car have 73,000 miles original but the previous owner did some work on it... he install a cam, a performance chip that have the fuel cut-off eliminated... my car is still a project in which it's sitting in different color on body panels... I am running 17 inch all around...have a custom ram air that I made... a molded GTR wing with a adjustable blade... a pisa taillight with corvettes lights on it... a mecham scoop...I also installed a factory sunroof..I was going for the T-Top but it's too expensive... and I just came back from FOCOA and bought a Kid Danger Air Dam for the Gt fascia... My freind Keith has the Miller Woods Turbo for the fiero in his garage and I already made an offer to buy it in which he agreed...can't tell you how much but alot cheaper than Design One Systems...For those who doesn't know Miller Woods Turbo... they are the company who started the well proven turbo for  the Fiero... The owner of Design One Systems  is the the same guy who work for Miller Woods Turbo....I will do the turbo charging once I get my engine converted to the 3.4 camaro block...co'z this block is ribbed up for strength...and durability...I like the Fiero's alot....a freind of mine thinks it's a poor mans ferrari....oh well....
Z||000027||SCCA FIERO||09-02-99||11:46 PM||||Hello, my name is Chris and I live in Ogden, Utah. I am 27 and I am a General Contractor. <p>When I was 15 or 16, my brother bought a silver 86SE V6 4spd Fiero. I bought it from him in 1991. Not too long ago I bought an 88 coupe to replace the beat up 86. I put the V6, dash, gauges and the options from the 86. I also installed the spoiler and added a set of 87GT wheels painted black. I also shortened the shifter and added a 120mph speedo and I am now in the process of turbocharging this Fiero.<p>This year I got hooked on autocrossing with the local SCCA club. <p>
