Z||000049||DXR_MOM||09-04-99||09:06 PM||||Well, I guess it our turn meaning DXR_DAD and myself DXR_MOM.  DAD is 39 and MOM is 37.  Our baby is a 86SE 4-speed, Black w/gray interior.  For all of you who want to know what DXR stands for here it is (Dimension X Racing & Auto Sports), our baby has 75,000 original miles and some of the mods are as follows:  K&N Cone, Modified Intake (our design), Port & Re-weld Exhaust manifolds, MSD Controller, MSD Coil, Accel 300 wires, Dyno Max Super-Flow Cat., Gorlic Stock Exhaust System, Power Pulleys, Non-Stock Reartail, Rear Deck Lid Scoop, Shortened Shifter, Polished Stock Rims, 100 Watt EQ Stock Stereo and JBL Speakers.  We live in South San Francisco, California, and have had our baby we call (Black Beauty ) for 3 years.<p>DXR <p>
Z||000050||Shaun41178||09-05-99||01:50 AM||||Hi everyone!<p>My name is Shaun Hammitt.  I was born on 4/11/78 which make me 21 yrs old.  I am currently a student at the University of Toledo majoring in Law enforcement.  I would like to make a Federal Branch of the Justice dept. someday i.e. FBI or DEA.  I was born here in Toledo OH as well which is located in NW Ohio.  I have no kids nor a girlfreind as i am not very attractive for if I was I would have a girlfriend.  Makes sense right?  i like to make people luagh<p>I bought my red 85 Gt auto back when I was a senior in HS.  I saved up two years to get one and finally found one at a decent price with 91k miles on it.  Drove it for a year 9k miles till a rod bearing decided to make noise right at 100k miles on it.  pretty wierd if you ask me.  Pulled the engine out without any prior mechanical experience.  Found a almost new engine for $135 and installed it and then threw nitrous on it and have had the nitrous on it for a year now.  Other mods include pulley custom intake with K&N cone, ported exhasut manifolds and Crane ign and coil with accel wires, and rear sway bar.<p>This board RULES!!!!<p>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178
Z||000051||Bozone||09-05-99||09:46 AM||||Yeah, I thought I'd qualify as oldest here but Dick beat me out by 2-1/2 years. My name is Fred Clarke, I'm 59, a self-employed computer publishing person and have 3 Fieros - one of which I bought new in 87. I live in East Greenwich, Rhode Island. Present project car is a puff red 86.5 GT that slid on ice into a tree. Plan total restore on it and it's at Fiero Factory right now. Goodtaknowya!!
Z||000052||theogre||09-05-99||12:07 PM||||The Ogre, AKA Ogre King.<br>male age 306<br>Master of all things in Ravenwood Swamp.<p>I have a real problem with threads like this.<p>Sorry, call it paranoid,,,, I don't post any more personal information than absolutly required in public places. I don't have a specific problem with any of our members, but I'm probly more aware of some of the security risks of the internet than many of you are. I've been involved with cars for a long time, electronics and computers even longer. I've seen first hand a number of security problems caused by very simple "social engineering" and spoofing legitimat systems. You'd be very frightened what can be done with the little information some of you have posted above already. Some of you have already posted enough information that people I've known could easily obtain your driving record, SSI number, Credit card data, and half a hundred other things.<p>As Cliff has said,,, there are around 400 registered users. There is no way to include those who simply surf the site periodically. Any of those people could lift this whole thread and use it to rob people blind. Please be carefull what you post about yourself both in the forum and in your profiles.<p>That said:::::<p>Dave<br>delaWhere??? RI is smaller but not by bloody much.<br>37<p>87 SC 4<p>What else,,,, I fix stuff to feed my face. cars, computers, whatever. Any one in the Delaware Valley need their house wired for a LAN? I know I can't be the only one here with several computers and a couple printers.
Z||000053||Patrick||09-05-99||01:03 PM||||<br>The Ogre has spoken...<br>Geez, you're only 37 years old? <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15> <p>I have to agree with you about the personal information that people post about themselves on the 'net. I didn't want to appear "unfriendly", but I purposely didn't include my last name earlier because of the same fears that you have stated.<p> 
Z||000054||Cliff Pennock||09-05-99||01:07 PM||||Well, I wouldn't call it paranoid Ogre - but it's close! <IMG SRC="/ubb/wink.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>Seriously, before people stop posting alltogether: there isn't any harm in posting name, age and occupation. I haven't seen any security codes from alarm systems together with home addresses and holiday schedules posted yet. None of us are listed in Forbes 500 (at least last time I checked) so it's not like we're a prime target for hustlers...
Z||000055||Cliff Pennock||09-05-99||01:12 PM||||Besided - there are <b>a lot</b> of other places on the internet where people can easily access this information. If you have an internet account your full name, address, telephone-number, etc. can be found within minutes.
