Z||000068||theogre||09-09-1999||02:45 PM||||Geeze.... not even one guess?<P>What album did Roxette release, nearly completely, to the promo?  Crash Boom Bang was released short a couple songs.<P>What fast food chain carried the promo? Mc Donnalds. You got one of 4-5 CD's with a food purchase for about 4$ more.<P>Why was the promo controversial? The record companies where peaved that the price of the CD was about 4$us. While the rest of the CD's where rereleased material, Crash Boom Bang was a brand new album. Much of the sales numbers for the album came from the McD's promo. This was a signifigant bite of the record lables proffit. Mc D's pretty much told the record companies to stuff it, but they've never done this type promo again.<BR>||||reg||
Z||000069||lowCG||09-09-1999||11:17 PM||||So,who sold the rights to McD's?<BR>Are they on the bottom of the East river?||||reg||
Z||000070||Standard||09-10-1999||03:22 AM||||Hey All..  My name is Mike Nendza.  I live I Golden Valley, MN not too far from Minneapolis and I drive a beat-up red 84 sport coupe.  The reason that it's beat up is that I don't have enough money or connections to get it looking good (hint, hint..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But next spring I'm going to be looking for an 87 or 88 GT.. well, any GT as long as it runs good and looks decent and I can afford it!<BR>catch ya later||||reg||
