Z||000123||007DOUG||03-13-2000||07:18 PM||||Doug Kinney, Christian, 26 years young, but act like I'm 12. <P>Wheeling, West Virginia. 7 hours from BS degrees in Chemistry, Philosophy, and Religion.<P>Tried the chemistry lab job already and I hated  it. I wanted to work for the EPA, but realized I use common sense and reasoning and they don't.<P>So, I'll stick to my passion of driving. Currently employeed by UPS, pizza delivery "boy", and bulk mail driver. And yes, with three jobs I still have weekends off to drive and show my fieros.<P> I currently have 11 fieros ranging from pace cars to 88 GT's. Visit my website and click on "my garage" to view them and their description.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse</A> <P>I live by two mottos:<P>#1 Everyday above ground is a good day.<BR>#2 Time is both my most precious, and most perishable of all possesions.<P>And for all the ladies out there, I'm single. (you can thank my ex-fiancee for that)<P>...........Doug<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000124||zebrex||03-13-2000||10:39 PM||||My name is Trent Dufour Im 27 from jasonville Indiana. I am working as a network administrator for a local ISP while pursuing my mcse (Then I can get a real job).<BR>I use to bulid custom jeeps for offroading but my boss had an 88 formula broke down in his garage for the last year and a half . He told me three hundred bucks and get the **** thing out of his garage. All it took to get it running was a starter and a battery and now im struggling with a brake job, but man am I hooked I cant leave the thing alone, and its in great shape 44000 miles and the air still works.||||reg||1
Z||000125||frontal lobe||03-13-2000||11:12 PM||||Dan Thompson.  44 years old.  I love cars but over the years I have only been able to drive them as I had to spend almost every waking minute studying to be a doctor.  I'm using the name frontal lobe because that's the part of the brain where intelligent thought is supposed to be formed, and the part my wife thinks needs examining since I have bought an '86GT and an '87GT in the past 6 months.  I bought an LT1 out of '96 Buick Roadmaster-30000miles.  It's going into the '87GT via a v8Archie kit.  One slight problem--I've never even changed the oil on a car before.  Oh well, not going to let minor details dissuade me.  Plus, I have a great friend who is going to help me (i.e. do it while I stand there, watch, and hand him tools!)  Hey, come on, it's a kit, how hard can it be?  I'll let you know in a year or two when it's finished!  P.S.  Any bets on how many parts are left over when I'm done that should be on somewhere?||||reg||1
